1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:04,800
Welcome to ARES-Health, an offline Safe Rust
medical decision workstation for deep space.

2
00:00:04,900 --> 00:00:09,800
On a Mars transit, radio round-trip delays
of 8 to 48 minutes break cloud telemedicine.

3
00:00:09,900 --> 00:00:14,800
We launch ARES-MedOS locally with zero
external network calls or cloud APIs.

4
00:00:14,900 --> 00:00:19,800
The status bar tracks 4 ARINC-653 partitions,
128-byte CRC-32C binary frames, and Mars OWLT.

5
00:00:19,900 --> 00:00:24,800
In Act I, GATHER replays PhysioNet BIDMC v1.0.0
at 1 Hz, verified by SHA-256 against MANIFEST.

6
00:00:24,900 --> 00:00:29,800
The 13 missing PULSE and SpO2 samples stay
strictly null, never fabricated as zeros.

7
00:00:29,900 --> 00:00:34,800
Because 1 Hz numerics lack R-R intervals,
RMSSD displays BEAT_INTERVALS_NOT_AVAILABLE

8
00:00:34,900 --> 00:00:38,000
and raises DATA_DEGRADED_MISSING_CHANNELS.

9
00:00:38,100 --> 00:00:43,000
In Act II, we enable the What-If overlay
to stress-test 180 days of microgravity.

10
00:00:43,100 --> 00:00:48,000
Dropping ARED resistive load to 30% and
raising CO2 triggers a sub-millisecond pass.

11
00:00:48,100 --> 00:00:53,000
Notice the 1 Hz BIDMC replay cursor remains
immutable beneath the simulated What-If layer.

12
00:00:53,100 --> 00:00:58,000
In EVALUATE, the 3D UBERON heatmap reflects
soleus unloading and cephalic congestion.

13
00:00:58,100 --> 00:01:03,000
Our RK4 Sclerostin ODE and Hagen-Poiseuille
equation compute exact CGS jugular shear stress.

14
00:01:03,100 --> 00:01:08,000
NQS-STL evaluates rolling margins in O(1)
amortized time using Lemire's monotonic wedge.

15
00:01:08,100 --> 00:01:12,500
Timestral produces monotone quantile cones
q05 <= q50 <= q95 via stable softplus heads,

16
00:01:12,600 --> 00:01:15,000
explicitly marked ILLUSTRATIVE_SCENARIO_RANGE.

17
00:01:15,100 --> 00:01:20,000
In Act III, ACT selects Type-1 crystallized
MedOps Playbooks #01 through #05 under 20 us.

18
00:01:20,100 --> 00:01:25,000
Three deterministic Hard Clinical Safety
Gates guard every countermeasure action.

19
00:01:25,100 --> 00:01:30,000
Safety Gate 1 locks anticoagulants whenever
jugular thrombus is not POCUS-confirmed.

20
00:01:30,100 --> 00:01:35,000
Confirming a B-mode thrombus transitions the
Bayesian observer above 0.92 and unlocks #02.

21
00:01:35,100 --> 00:01:40,000
Safety Gate 2 monitors -30 mmHg LBNP and
auto-vents to 0 mmHg on pre-syncope triggers.

22
00:01:40,100 --> 00:01:45,000
Safety Gate 3 detects Martian 0.38g gait
asymmetry above 12% and adds +25% suit damping.

23
00:01:45,100 --> 00:01:50,000
All crew overrides are recorded in a
SHA-256 hash chain with ChaCha20-Poly1305 AEAD.

24
00:01:50,100 --> 00:01:55,000
In Act IV, pressing Alt+Space opens the
FastMCP command palette across 8 tools.

25
00:01:55,100 --> 00:02:00,000
query_dataset_graph searches 24 cataloged
sources and 110 Biolink nodes in microseconds.

26
00:02:00,100 --> 00:02:05,000
explain_biomarker_path traces OSD-818 to
heart rate while staying under 600 bytes.

27
00:02:05,100 --> 00:02:10,000
Untrusted telemetry is wrapped in XML tags
to prevent indirect prompt injection attacks.

28
00:02:10,100 --> 00:02:15,000
The air-gapped Voice Copilot summarizes state
without ever touching ODEs or safety gates.

29
00:02:15,100 --> 00:02:20,000
If no local LLM is running, a deterministic
Type-1 template copilot responds in <400 us.

30
00:02:20,100 --> 00:02:25,000
Each 128-byte Seqlock frame reads at 42 ns p50
with zero garbage collection pauses.

31
00:02:25,100 --> 00:02:32,000
And 900 Martian Sols of longitudinal history
compact into less than 200 KB via Welford.

32
00:02:32,100 --> 00:02:38,000
In Act V, we highlight scientific honesty:
scenario models stay ILLUSTRATIVE_UNVALIDATED.

33
00:02:38,100 --> 00:02:44,000
Phase 33 enforces subject-disjoint CQR
calibration before any clinical status upgrade.

34
00:02:44,100 --> 00:02:50,000
Running build_submission_docs.sh verifies our
7-slide Typst PDF, subtitles, and audit rules.

35
00:02:50,100 --> 00:02:55,000
8 Safe Rust crates, zero panics in production,
and dual MIT or Apache-2.0 open-source license.

36
00:02:55,100 --> 00:02:59,400
ARES-Health: Gather, Evaluate, Act.
Autonomous medical software for Moon to Mars.
